   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "poole/LUK.20.9#p1-bef4289c",
     "text": "Ver. 9-18. We met with this parable at large both in Mat 21:33-41, and in Mar 12:1-11. Its obvious scope is to let them know, that God in righteous judgment, for the Jews’ abusing the Lord’s prophets, John the Baptist, and himself, who was in a few days to be killed by them, would unchurch and destroy them, and raise up to himself a church amongst the Gentiles; and that this was no more than was prophesied of, Psa 118:22.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 21:33-41",
       "ref": "MAT.21.33-41"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 12:1-11",
       "ref": "MRK.12.1-11"
      },
      {
       "text": "Psa 118:22",
       "ref": "PSA.118.22"
      }
     ]
