  {
   "id": "poole/LUK.20.41",
   "range": "LUK.20.41",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "22215e74",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "poole/LUK.20.41#p1-ef9d35c0",
     "text": "Ver. 41-44. The answer had been easy if the scribes and Pharisees, who (Matthew saith) were there also, had owned Christ to be the Son of God. But this they did not own, and so, as Mat 22:46 tells us,",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 22:46",
       "ref": "MAT.22.46"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/LUK.20.41#p2-eef265f5",
     "text": "Thus Christ nonplussed all his adversaries.",
     "anchor": "No man was able to answer him a word, neither durst any man from that day forth ask him any more questions"
    }
   ]
  },
